# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, private.
#
# There is a Dockerfile in the repository that runs server.py, and it does
# `COPY . .`. Without this file that copies every local SQLite database into the
# image -- including the rows of test registrations -- along with anything else
# lying in the working tree. An image is published where it can be pulled.
#
# The Dockerfile is not what render.yaml deploys: the platform is served as a
# static site from firebase-public, and the data is in Firestore. The Dockerfile
# is kept for running server.py locally in a container.

# the databases, and anything holding personal data
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
uploads/
intercept-roots/
tools/tests/out/
dist/

# secrets and local settings
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log*
*-debug.log*

# version control and tooling noise
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
node_modules/

# the source tree, since the deployable copy is what is published
tools/
istimara/
sw.js
server.py
package.json
package-lock.json
README.md
DEPLOY.md
render.yaml
Dockerfile

# keep these: they are what the browser loads
# firebase-public/
# index.html
# app.js
# styles.css
# firebase-config.js
# firebase-adapter.js
# manifest.webmanifest
# assets/
# istimara/ -- served under firebase-public/istimara, so the copy that matters is
#             inside firebase-public and is not matched by the rule above
